{
  "_doc": "Single source of truth for county GTFS feeds. BOTH consumers read this file: the app (connectors/transit/feeds.ts) and the nightly pipeline (cce-transit-tables/preprocess.mjs). Keys are canonical lowercase-with-spaces; each consumer normalizes as it needs. These previously lived in two hand-synced registries with different key styles, so a drift surfaced as the Mac and the edge disagreeing about a site's transit \u2014 the hardest kind of bug to notice.",
  "notWired": {
    "imperial": "No published GTFS feed found in the Mobility Database catalog.",
    "alameda": "AC Transit \u2014 the county's primary operator \u2014 publishes GTFS only through api.actransit.org (401 without a token) and 511.org (API key); its open-data zips are archived snapshots whose last (Aug 2025) calendar ended 2025-12-06. Wiring BART, Emery Go-Round and LAVTA without it would report Oakland/Berkeley/Hayward bus sites as unserved. Verified 2026-09-15.",
    "alpine": "No GTFS feed exists: not in the Mobility Database catalog, the Transitland atlas, or Cal-ITP\u2019s monthly feed reports (2026-09-15).",
    "colusa": "No GTFS feed exists for Colusa County Transit: not in the Mobility Database catalog, the Transitland atlas, or Cal-ITP\u2019s monthly feed reports; the Trillium slug colusa-ca-us is a 404 (2026-09-15).",
    "del norte": "Redwood Coast Transit's only published feed (Trillium delnorte-ca-us, the URL Transitland and Cal-ITP still point at) parses but its calendar ended 2025-10-08 \u2014 342 days stale at wiring time, beyond the 120-day limit. Re-check when the agency republishes (2026-09-15).",
    "sierra": "No GTFS feed exists: not in the Mobility Database catalog, the Transitland atlas, or Cal-ITP\u2019s monthly feed reports (2026-09-15).",
    "tehama": "TRAX's only published feed (Trillium tehama-ca-us) has a calendar that ended 2019-01-09 \u2014 seven years stale. Not wired until the agency republishes (2026-09-15)."
  },
  "_gaps": {
    "_doc": "Wired counties whose registry is knowingly incomplete, so a \"no transit\" result near one of these operators is read as a gap in coverage rather than a fact. Each was checked 2026-09-15.",
    "contra costa": "Tri Delta Transit (East County: Antioch, Pittsburg, Brentwood, Oakley) publishes only via 511.org (API key). County Connection, WestCAT and BART are wired.",
    "kern": "Taft Area Transit and Ridgecrest Transit publish only static document uploads (no refreshable URL); Wasco is a flex feed. GET, Kern Transit, Delano and Arvin are wired.",
    "madera": "Madera Metro (City of Madera) \u2014 Trillium feed calendar ended 2024-02-07 and Cal-ITP's Aug 2026 report still lists that source. Only Madera County Connection (which also serves the city) is wired.",
    "placer": "Auburn Transit publishes only a static document upload (6 stops). Placer County Transit, TART and Roseville are wired.",
    "solano": "Fairfield and Suisun Transit (FAST) and Vacaville City Coach publish only via 511.org (API key); their Trillium feeds ended 2025-07 and 2026-02. Rio Vista Delta Breeze\u2019s feed ended 2021. Only SolTrans (Vallejo/Benicia) is wired.",
    "sonoma": "Petaluma Transit publishes only via 511.org (API key). Sonoma County Transit, Santa Rosa CityBus and SMART are wired.",
